p;utm_term=0_-736e5667b3-62240358</guid><pubDate>Wed, 23 Jul 2025 15:56:24 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title><![CDATA[Norwegian sovereign wealth fund deploys AI]]></title><description><![CDATA[<p><img src="https://pbs.twimg.com/media/GwYkpbdaYAEWX5f.jpg:large"></p><p>Karl Mehta (@karlmehta) on X</p><p>BREAKING: Norway’s $2 trillion wealth fund ran a 12-month AI experiment. They gave Claude access to their entire investment workflow. Result: 213,000 hours saved. 20% productivity boost. But what they found hiding in the data changed everything: A Thread 🧵</p><p>URL: <a href="https://x.com/karlmehta/status/1947284189461782807">https://x.com/karlmehta/status/1947284189461782807</a></p><p>source: <a href="https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2025/07/wednesday-assorted-links-512.html?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=wednesday-assorted-links-512">Wednesday assorted links</a></p>]]></description><link>https://x.com/karlmehta/status/1947284189461782807</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://x.com/karlmehta/status/1947284189461782807</guid><pubDate>Wed, 23 Jul 2025 15:56:24 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title><![CDATA[more thinking is not always good for the AI]]></title><description><![CDATA[<p><img src="https://pbs.twimg.com/media/Gwc8g2HbEAMiyy1.jpg:large"></p><p>Aryo Pradipta Gema (@aryopg) on X</p><p>New Anthropic Research: “Inverse Scaling in Test-Time Compute” We found cases where longer reasoning leads to lower accuracy.
Our findings suggest that naïve scaling of test-time compute may inadvertently reinforce problematic reasoning patterns. 🧵</p><p>URL: <a href="https://x.com/aryopg/status/1947591901886222570">https://x.com/aryopg/status/1947591901886222570</a></p><p>source: <a href="https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2025/07/wednesday-assorted-links-512.html?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=wednesday-assorted-links-512">Wednesday assorted links</a></p>]]></description><link>https://x.com/aryopg/status/1947591901886222570</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://x.com/aryopg/status/1947591901886222570</guid><pubDate>Wed, 23 Jul 2025 15:56:24 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title><![CDATA[Some Amish settlements have TFR above 10]]></title><description><![CDATA[<p><img src="https://pbs.twimg.com/media/Gwfa93YXQAEh7of.jpg:large"></p><p>Max (@ComteWasRight) on X</p><p>Donnermeyer released another Amish fertility study. The paper compares completed fertility across four Swiss Amish settlements. The value for Seymour and California Corners settlements is over 10! Adams county at 9.3. The most liberal of the four, Allen County, measured at ~7.5.</p><p>URL: <a href="https://x.com/ComteWasRight/status/1947771903302639826">https://x.com/ComteWasRight/status/1947771903302639826</a></p><p>source: <a href="https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2025/07/wednesday-assorted-links-512.html?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=wednesday-assorted-links-512">Wednesday assorted links</a></p>]]></description><link>https://x.com/ComteWasRight/status/1947771903302639826</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://x.com/ComteWasRight/status/1947771903302639826</guid><pubDate>Wed, 23 Jul 2025 15:56:24 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title><![CDATA[Colombia is now at 1.2]]></title><description><![CDATA[<p><img src="https://pbs.twimg.com/media/GweO_XmWwAAFoqE.jpg:large"></p><p>More Births (@MoreBirths) on X</p><p>Colombia has had one of the fastest fertility drops in the world, from 2.57 births/woman in 2000 all the way down to 1.2 in 2024. How can it be that Colombia, with a GDP of 7K per year, has a fertility so much lower than the US? And why is this happening across Latin America? 🧵</p><p>URL: <a href="https://x.com/MoreBirths/status/1947733910177075582">https://x.com/MoreBirths/status/1947733910177075582</a></p><p>source: <a href="https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2025/07/wednesday-assorted-links-512.html?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=wednesday-assorted-links-512">Wednesday assorted links</a></p>]]></description><link>https://x.com/MoreBirths/status/1947733910177075582</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://x.com/MoreBirths/status/1947733910177075582</guid><pubDate>Wed, 23 Jul 2025 15:56:24 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title><![CDATA[coupling rate vs. fertility rate]]></title><description><![CDATA[<p><img src="https://pbs.twimg.com/media/GwhLKD5bEAMO9CA.jpg:large"></p><p>J. Sanilac (@Sanilac_J) on X</p><p>For reasons I don’t understand, fertility experts routinely talk past an elephant in the room: the declining birthrate is downstream of declining relationship formation. I suppose “selfish couples who hate babies” are a more respectable topic than the death of romance (and sex)?</p><p>URL: <a href="https://x.com/sanilac_j/status/1947891572366053812?s=46">https://x.com/sanilac_j/status/1947891572366053812?s=46</a></p><p>source: <a href="https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2025/07/wednesday-assorted-links-512.html?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=wednesday-assorted-links-512">Wednesday assorted links</a></p>]]></description><link>https://x.com/sanilac_j/status/1947891572366053812?s=46</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://x.com/sanilac_j/status/1947891572366053812?s=46</guid><pubDate>Wed, 23 Jul 2025 15:56:24 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title><![CDATA[Deep in the Berkshires, just off the Mohawk Trail, in an abandoned strip mall anchored by an erstwhile Price Chopper, awaits a sleek, smart prod